If global i18n exists, convert these to en.json/vi.json keys under footer.* and call t('footer.about') etc.

8) QA Checklist

 Footer renders on all pages that use layout.tsx, appears once per page.

 No logo stretching; social icons align baseline.

 Columns match the content map; all links are focusable with visible ring.

 Vietnamese by default; English strings render when lang='en'.

 Responsive: desktop (≥1200px) shows all columns; tablet shows 3-column grid; mobile shows 2-column grid.

 No inline hex colors in JSX; colors from base.css.

 Lighthouse a11y ≥ 90.

9) Tasks for Cursor (explicit)

Task 1 — Create component

Create src/components/site/Footer.tsx implementing the structure in Section 6 with all columns/links from Section 2. Use nav/section semantics and i18n keys.

Task 2 — Add styles

Append the CSS from Section 6 to src/styles/base.css. Reuse tokens; do not introduce new colors.

Task 3 — Wire into layout

Import and place <Footer /> in src/app/layout.tsx just before the closing body.

Task 4 — i18n

If global i18n exists, add footer keys to en.json/vi.json. Otherwise, create src/components/site/footer.i18n.{en,vi}.ts and a tiny useT() inside Footer that reads from the global context or falls back to local dictionaries.

Task 5 — Assets

Add /public/tuto-logo.svg and social SVGs in /public/icons/. Use height:32px; width:auto for logo.

Task 6 — Verify

Provide screenshots at 1440px, 1024px, and 390px widths. Confirm keyboard focus and responsive